        "degree_identity": "BS Artificial Intelligence and Decision Making,Course6-4. Current chart and explicitly cohort-qualified6-4_2025 view remain distinct; source list-term conflict not resolved.",
        "required_and_choices": "The actual6-4_2025 Required subjects section has a bare6.1200 discrete-math row, two explicit One of math rows, and both6.1010/6.1210 foundation subjects. Three identities are fixed: two foundations plus one mathematics. Five Center subject selections retain bundled options and the seven designation overlays are not extra slots. An independent source reconstruction records all versioned required/options/contextual identity sets separately; chart/GIR/HASS full-profile work remains in progress.",
        "elective_pools": "Versioned lists and39 HASS field inventories were previously mapped; subject and applicability second pass remains ongoing. Existing source questions are preserved.",
        "prerequisites": "All 248 annotated versioned subjects were read, preserving exact prerequisite/corequisite fields and separately noted recommended preparation, enrollment restrictions and conditional registration. The C01/C51 lecture/module pairs have explicit completion conditions for credit; these do not become extra universal fixed courses. CC.1803 and ES.1803 are cohort-limited. Special topics need term-specific departmental information. Remaining source-view/GIR/HASS prerequisites still require review. The official notation explicitly permits instructor permission when stated prerequisites are unmet; this conditional route grants no individual approval. Departmental calculus prerequisites, split-sequence registration/credit, chemistry intended preparation versus formal None and biology lottery limits are separately represented. Mathematics prohibits first-year graduate enrollment.",
        "credits_and_units": "The current catalog Subjects notation explicitly defines total credit as the sum of the three numeric unit components. All 248 annotated versioned rows now have observed MIT-unit totals; 13 absent annotations remain null. Generic special-topic zero values are literal printed observations, not proof of current topic/offering. The 6.4300 chart/CI-M conflict remains separate. No conversion to semester hours.",
        "classification": "All 261 versioned subject records have manual dispositions: 248 have actual annotations, including nine generic special-subject descriptions that do not establish content; 13 have no annotation. Mathematical optimization and probability remain distinct from AI methods and computer systems. Physical engineering and human cognition remain domain content. Mixed methods/domains remain other with explicit candidates. All 845 HASS, 63 unversioned chart/reference and 20 GIR rows still require their separate evidence review. Twelve GIR rows now have separately read departmental descriptions: five calculus, four biology and three chemistry. Biology variant instructor labels span Fall2025/Spring2026 and are not current offering claims. The63 separate unversioned chart/CI-M records were reread against actual source tables:39 precise-title classifications and24 unclassified titles. These are explicitly limited title reviews, not descriptions or inherited versioned metadata.",
